  "id": "COMPOUND:11768 - PROTEIN:922",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that anle138b may interact with the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 1E through multiple pathways. Path_120621 indicates that anle138b enhances the uterotonic activity of Dimethyltryptamine, which is known to bind to the 5-HT1E receptor. Path_120622 and Path_120623 show that anle138b increases the efficacy of lofexidine and Radium Ra 223 dichloride, both of which are known to target the 5-HT1E receptor. These findings collectively imply that anle138b may modulate the activity of the 5-HT1E receptor through the activation of compounds that bind to it. The evidence is consistent with the idea that anle138b could act as a modulator of the 5-HT1E receptor, either directly or via its effects on compounds that interact with it. The strength of the evidence is moderate, as the scores are relatively low, and further experimental validation would be needed to confirm the direct interaction between anle138b and the 5-HT1E receptor.",
